[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 457,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 370,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61695,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 35,
        "headingId": 370,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Clear cell borderline tumour (CCBT) is an adenofibromatous clear cell tumour with glandular crowding and low-grade nuclear atypia but no stromal invasion.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:38:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 458,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 371,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61696,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 35,
        "headingId": 371,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8313/1 Clear cell borderline tumour</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:38:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 459,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 372,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61697,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 35,
        "headingId": 372,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2C73.Y Other specified malignant neoplasms of the ovary</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:38:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 460,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61698,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 35,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> atypical proliferative clear cell tumour; clear cell tumour of low malignant potential</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:38:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61699,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 35,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:38:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61700,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 35,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Ovary</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:38:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61701,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 35,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients may present with symptoms of a pelvic mass, including increased abdominal girth and pelvic pain, or the tumour may be an incidental finding.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:38:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61702,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 35,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Pure CCBTs account for &lt;&nbsp;1% of all ovarian borderline tumours {22622950} and are rarely found as the exclusive element in a tumour. In all other cases, CCBTs are components of clear cell carcinoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:38:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61703,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 35,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:38:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61704,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 35,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most patients are postmenopausal {22622950; 21479128; 4052962; 6692303}. Clear cell adenofibroma and CCBT are typically present in combination and are sometimes associated with endometriosis. CCBTs that accompany clear cell carcinoma show genetic changes similar to those of the carcinomatous component, including <em>PIK3CA</em> and <em>ARID1A</em> abnormalities {22157930; 22120431}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:38:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61705,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 35,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>CCBTs are solid or predominantly solid, with small to large cysts and a firm white, tan, or grey cut surface. The mean size is 6&nbsp;cm {22622950; 21479128; 4052962; 6692303}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:38:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61706,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 35,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Variably sized glands, embedded in a fibromatous stroma, contain low cuboidal or flat cells with enlarged nuclei, sometimes with nucleoli. The cells have clear or eosinophilic cytoplasm. Mitotic activity is low. The glands are more irregular and crowded, and less uniform in size, than in adenofibroma. Minimal nuclear stratification is permitted, but densely aggregated glands and papillary or tubulocystic architecture are absent by definition.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:38:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61707,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 35,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>If the tumour is ruptured or there is surface involvement, peritoneal fluid cytology may show epithelial aggregates with nuclear enlargement and overlapping, as well as conspicuous nucleoli.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:38:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61708,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 35,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:38:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61709,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 35,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Essential:</em> adenofibromatous clear cell tumour with glandular crowding, nuclear atypia, and a low mitotic count; no stromal invasion or papillary architecture.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-02T17:49:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61710,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 35,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "<p>CCBT is staged according to the Union for International Cancer Control (UICC) TNM classification (see <em>TNM staging of ovarian, fallopian tube, and primary peritoneal carcinoma</em>&nbsp;[[Brierley JD, Gospodarowicz MK, Wittekind C, editors. TNM classification of malignant tumours. 8th ed. Oxford (UK): Wiley-Blackwell; 2017.]]) and the FIGO staging system.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-15T11:06:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61711,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 35,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There have been no reported recurrences {22622950; 4052962; 6692303}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T16:38:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]